## Real defects

- **P1 — Elevated tiers lose mandatory reviewer requirements under `--base`.** `_pending_elevation()` returns only a commit SHA based on human approval, while the effective tier remains derived solely from paths/report. The SHA is passed only as `inherited_human_gate`, so an elevated L3 ancestor can ultimately pass with an L1 report containing tests and human approval—but no Codex or GLM evidence. An already-approved elevated report is ignored even if its required reviews never ran. A direct logic reproduction returned success with checks for only tests and human approval. [bin/coverloop:337](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:337), [bin/coverloop:341](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:341), [bin/coverloop:2158](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2158), [bin/coverloop:2251](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2251)

- **P1 — The default reviewer packet may omit earlier unverified commits being classified.** Without `--base`, classification spans from the last validated baseline through HEAD, but `COVERLOOP_DIFF` contains only `git show HEAD`. Thus an unreviewed migration followed by a harmless commit derives L3, while both reviewers see only the harmless final commit; their transcripts are then recorded as evidence for the entire span. [bin/coverloop:516](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:516), [bin/coverloop:536](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:536), [bin/coverloop:2544](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2544)

- **P1 — The outside-worktree boundary remains bypassable through inherited search paths.** The reviewer environment copies `PATH`, `PYTHONPATH`, and similar variables unchanged. With the repository on `PYTHONPATH`, the stated `python3 -m reviewer` example still imports a planted repository `reviewer.py`; with a repository directory on `PATH`, a bare reviewer executable resolves there despite the scratch cwd. This recreates the self-reviewer forge the patch intends to close. [bin/coverloop:2549](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2549), [bin/coverloop:1037](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1037)

