  2345	    The whole transcript is read, not a tail window: a review that says FAIL and
  2346	    then emits 5 KB of appendix would otherwise have its failure scroll out of
  2347	    view. The closing-position rule is the other half of the same idea — a
  2348	    prompt echo containing the marker, followed by a review that never reaches a
  2349	    verdict, must not count as approval. The small allowance exists because real
  2350	    reviewers append a footer (Codex prints "tokens used" and a count after its
  2351	    reply); it is not room for review content.
